Z||000000||My7Fieros||09-30-2000||12:17 AM||||Ok, Im almost finished with the Formula restoration. However, every time I get her running just right, some little thing goes out. Heres some examples.. <BR>Pick up coil..around 20 bucks<BR>Ignition controle module..around 20 bucks    <BR>Oxygen sensor..around 20 bucks<BR>Coolant sensor..around 20 bucks<BR>Oil sending unit..around 20 bucks<BR>I A C..around 20 bucks<BR>Water pump..around 20 bucks<BR>Plug wires..around 20 bucks<BR>Temp. sensor..around 20 bucks<BR>Phew! Well, I FINALLY got her painted! I also put the body side moldings back on, quarter windows, yahda yahda yahda..only a couple more things to do...Im taking her to get a new cat converter (theres not one on it at all! it was like that when I bought it)..and new tire..neither of which is remotely close to 20 bucks...but no biggie.<BR>Well, I went to go take her on a short spin around the block, when guess what...the damn interior began to fog up and reek of antifreeze...HEATER CORE!!! And guess how much one costs....yup, around 20 bucks. Jeez!<BR>Oh well, none of these things have been a big deal..just seems funny how all these little parts are somewhere in the 20 dollar range (most all came from Autozone).<BR>Anyway, I'll post pics prob next week of the before/after..you wont believe its the same car!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 09-30-2000).]||||reg||1
